**Subject: Request to Include *Essentials of Medical Device Clinical Resear=
ch* in Your Institutional Library and Training Resources**

Dear **[Director/Dean/Head of Department/Procurement Officer]**,

The medical-technology industry is entering a defining phase. MedTech has e=
merged as a **sunrise sector**, driven by advances in medical devices, diag=
nostics, digital health, artificial intelligence, robotics, connected techn=
ologies, and indigenous innovation. India=92s opportunity is vast=97but rea=
lising this potential will require more than technology alone. It will requ=
ire a strong ecosystem of clinical evidence, regulatory capability, risk-ba=
sed decision-making, and professionally trained human resources. [assets.kp=
mg](https://assets.kpmg.com/content/dam/kpmgsites/in/pdf/2023/10/from-volum=
e-to-value.pdf)

One of the most pressing challenges facing the sector is the scarcity of sp=
ecialised resources. Institutions and organisations need professionals who =
can understand not only device design and engineering, but also clinical in=
vestigation, regulatory pathways, quality systems, risk management, medical=
 writing, data interpretation, safety reporting, and post-marketing surveil=
lance. Industry and policy reports have identified gaps in the availability=
 and quality of skilled personnel across biomedical engineering, quality as=
surance, clinical research, regulatory affairs, and related technical funct=
ions. [pharma-dept.gov](https://pharma-dept.gov.in/sites/default/files/Fina=
l%20Boosting%20of%20Medical%20Devices%20Industry%20-%20Report%20-%202023.pd=
f)

In this context, we are pleased to present:

## *Essentials of Medical Device Clinical Research*
### By Dr. Ashish Indani

This comprehensive multi-volume reference has been developed to address the=
 growing knowledge and capability gap in the medical-device ecosystem. It b=
rings together the essential scientific, clinical, regulatory, operational,=
 and post-market aspects of medical-device clinical research in one structu=
red resource.

The book covers a wide range of subjects, including:

- Medical-device clinical research principles and methodologies.
- Global regulatory frameworks, pathways, standards, and submission require=
ments.
- Clinical investigation planning, protocol development, and study executio=
n.
- Clinical evaluation and clinical-evaluation reports.
- Risk management, safety assessment, and benefit=96risk analysis.
- Clinical operations, medical writing, data management, and biostatistics.
- Ethics, patient protection, safety reporting, and quality oversight.
- Preclinical research, diagnostic devices, and software-based medical devi=
ces.
- Materiovigilance and post-marketing clinical follow-up.
- Post-market surveillance and the continuing generation of real-world evid=
ence.
- The roles and responsibilities of sponsors, investigators, research teams=
, regulatory professionals, and other stakeholders.

The book is designed to serve as a practical bridge between **academic lear=
ning and industry application**. It can support medical-device, biomedical,=
 pharmacy, biotechnology, and clinical-research programmes, while also serv=
ing as a valuable reference for hospitals, research institutions, start-ups=
, manufacturers, regulatory teams, clinical-affairs departments, and profes=
sional training centres.

For students, it provides a structured introduction to a specialised and ra=
pidly expanding field. For faculty and researchers, it offers a consolidate=
d teaching and reference resource. For industry professionals, it supports =
the practical understanding required to plan better studies, prepare strong=
er clinical evidence, manage regulatory expectations, and protect patient s=
afety throughout the product lifecycle.

We therefore request your institution to consider purchasing copies of *Ess=
entials of Medical Device Clinical Research* for:

- Institutional and departmental libraries.
- Medical-device, biomedical, pharmacy, biotechnology, and clinical-researc=
h programmes.
- Clinical-affairs and regulatory-affairs teams.
- Faculty development and professional training initiatives.
- Research scholars, postgraduate students, and industry trainees.
- Institutional innovation, incubation, and technology-transfer centres.

Investing in this book is an investment in **knowledge infrastructure and w=
orkforce readiness**. As MedTech continues to expand, institutions that dev=
elop capable professionals will be better positioned to contribute to safe =
innovation, indigenous product development, global regulatory compliance, a=
nd improved patient outcomes.

We would be pleased to share further details regarding the volumes, ISBNs, =
pricing, institutional orders, and special arrangements for bulk purchase.

Thank you for your consideration. We look forward to your support in streng=
thening medical-device education, clinical research, and regulatory capabil=
ity.

Yours sincerely,

**[Name]**
**[Designation]**
**[Organisation/Publisher]**
**[Email Address]**
**[Phone Number]**
**[Website/Order Link]**

### Suggested closing line

**Let us equip the next generation of MedTech professionals with the knowle=
dge required to transform promising innovation into safe, clinically meanin=
gful, and globally acceptable medical technologies.**

